---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContactList from "../components/ContactList.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { talkPath, talks } from "../lib/talks";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="About — Software Security"
    description="Andrew Lilley Brinker is a Member of Technical Staff at Anthropic, writing about software security, memory safety, Rust, and open source."
    socialImage="/social/about.png"
    socialImageAlt="About — Software Security"
>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <div
        class="about-photo-frame inline-block relative group max-w-36 md:max-w-48 transition-transform duration-300 rotate-3 hover:rotate-0 float-right ml-4 md:ml-8 mb-4 md:mb-8 -top-10"
    >
        <img
            src="/image/andrew.png"
            alt="Grayscale and dithered picture of Andrew"
            width="500"
            height="500"
            loading="eager"
            class="!m-0 rounded-md block"
        />
    </div>
    <p>
        I’m a Member of Technical Staff at <a href="https://www.anthropic.com"
            >Anthropic</a
        >.
    </p>
    <p>
        Before that I worked on software security, vulnerability management, and
        open source at <a href="https://www.mitre.org">MITRE</a>, where I led <a
            href="https://github.com/mitre/hipcheck">Hipcheck</a
        >, which helps maintainers and users assess dependency supply-chain risk
        via plugin-based analyses.
    </p>
    <p>
        I also worked on the <a href="https://www.cve.org/">CVE</a> system, improving
        authz&ThinSpace;/&ThinSpace;authn, introducing support for <a
            href="https://packageurl.org/">Package URLs</a
        > in CVE Records, and enhancing the processes of the Quality Working Group.
    </p>
    <p>
        I previously served on the <a href="https://omnibor.io/">OmniBOR</a> Core
        Team, including leading creation of the <a
            href="https://github.com/omnibor/omnibor-rs"
            >Rust library and omnibor CLI</a
        >.
    </p>
    <aside class="info-callout" aria-labelledby="my-name">
        <p id="my-name" class="info-callout-title">My Name</p>
        <p>
            “Lilley Brinker” is my full last name. Two parts, no hyphen. When my
            wife and I got married we combined our last names without a hyphen.
            My last name is not “Brinker” and it is not correct to call me “Mr.
            Brinker”.
        </p>
        <p>“Lilley” is pronounced like the word “lily”.</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="not-prose mt-16 mb-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <h2 id="work" class="font-sans text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted">Work</h2>
        <a
            href="/resume.pdf"
            class="inline-flex h-8 shrink-0 items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-neutral-500/10 pl-3.5 pr-2 font-sans text-sm text-neutral-600 hover:bg-neutral-500/15 hover:text-black dark:text-muted dark:hover:text-white"
            >Résumé <span class="tag">PDF</span></a
        >
    </div>
    <p>
        I want the people who build and maintain software to be able to make
        informed decisions about what they depend on. That is why I founded <a
            href="https://github.com/mitre/hipcheck">Hipcheck</a
        > and led its redesign as an extensible supply-chain analysis tool.
    </p>
    <p>
        I am drawn to work at the intersection of technical standards, public
        policy, and open source communities. I have advised federal software
        policy on SBOMs and open source security, and through <a
            href="https://omnibor.io">OmniBOR</a
        >, I worked on better ways to handle software identity.
    </p>
    <p>
        Memory safety matters to me because it makes software safer by default.
        In <a href="https://queue.acm.org/detail.cfm?id=3773095"
            >“Memory Safety for Skeptics”</a
        >, published in <em>ACM Queue</em> and <em>Communications of the ACM</em>,
        I make the case for pursuing it amid competing priorities. I have taught
        Rust at MITRE and programming language theory at <a
            href="https://cse.csusb.edu">CSUSB</a
        >, spoken at <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0PhfaFkzdBA">RustConf</a
        > and <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Wz2oFEDwiOk"
            >Rust Belt Rust</a
        >, contributed to the official Rust documentation and Rustonomicon, and
        edited <a
            href="https://www.manning.com/books/write-powerful-rust-macros"
            >a book on Rust procedural macros</a
        >.
    </p>
    <h3 id="talks" class="not-prose mt-12 mb-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted">Talks</h3>
    {
        talks.map((talk) => (
            <article class="mb-10">
                <h4 class="!m-0 !mb-1 !font-sans !text-lg !font-normal">
                    <a
                        class="group !no-underline text-black dark:text-white"
                        href={talkPath(talk)}
                    >
                        <span class="dither-underline">{talk.title}</span>
                    </a>
                </h4>
                <div class="flex gap-4 flex-wrap text-sm text-muted">
                    <span>
                        {talk.type === "panel"
                            ? "Participated in panel at"
                            : "Presented at"}{" "}
                        <a href={talk.event_link}>{talk.event}</a> on{" "}
                        {new Date(`${talk.date}T12:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString(
                            "en-US",
                            {
                                month: "long",
                                day: "numeric",
                                year: "numeric",
                                timeZone: "UTC",
                            },
                        )}
                    </span>
                    {talk.video_link && (
                        <span>
                            <a href={talk.video_link}>Watch the Recording</a>
                        </span>
                    )}
                    {talk.slides_link && (
                        <span>
                            <a href={talk.slides_link}>View the Slides</a>
                        </span>
                    )}
                </div>
                {talk.description && <p class="!mt-2">{talk.description}</p>}
            </article>
        ))
    }
    <h2 id="where-to-find-me" class="not-prose mt-16 mb-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted">Social / Contact</h2>
    <ContactList />
    <h2 id="ai-policy" class="not-prose mt-16 mb-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted">AI Policy</h2>
    <p>
        The words on this site were written by Andrew with care. Its design was
        implemented with the aid of AI. If AI-generated content is ever posted,
        it will be clearly identified.
    </p>
    <p>
        Disclosure: I work at Anthropic, which builds AI systems. Everything
        here is my own view, not my employer’s.
    </p>
</BaseLayout>
